  "description": "v66 validity retraining (Path B). Identical to the v65.1 paper curriculum except: candidateSamplingMode spatial_maximin, initialShelterMode demand_greedy, plannerShortlistObservation enriched (inert in training), actorPriorDeferMode below_sites. Full pooled State College and Spokane belief-rollout curriculum at 2,500 represented pedestrians per city. The public observation includes shelter-overrun risk, forecast displacement and safe-capacity coverage. Ten equal 300-person installations provide N-1 capacity resilience: any one failed shelter still leaves capacity for all 2,500 people. Stage E uses 20 random-reference episodes per city and Stage P uses 80 simulator-graded policy-improvement episodes per city. v65 changes compute only: a bit-identical vectorized belief-forecast kernel, the full regional observation built only at the first step, decision epochs and the terminal step, and a belief-trajectory memo shared by rollout candidates of the same future. Every simulated, observed and graded number equals v64 for the same seeds. v65.1 declares the base wind speed (16.67 m/min, previously passed as --override hazardWindSpeedMPerMinute=16.67) in the curriculum, so no launch-time override is needed or allowed.",
